            'faqs' => [
                ['How is this different from a general project management qualification?', '<p>Context, all the way through. Each of the six units is written for construction: the leadership unit is about organisational direction in construction project management, the planning unit is about integrated construction project planning, delivery and control, and the research unit sits in construction project management too. The specification also names live sector concerns such as building safety, information management and supply chain complexity, which a generic syllabus would not reach.</p>', 1],
                ['What does the assessment actually look like?', '<p>A Portfolio of Evidence, with no examination. You assemble evidence demonstrating that you meet the learning outcomes of each unit, drawing on real project work where you can. Your centre assesses and signs off each unit, an internal quality assurer verifies the judgements, and Gatehouse moderates externally before certification. Resubmission arrangements are covered by the awarding body\'s published centre policies.</p>', 2],
                ['Which jobs does it lead to?', '<p>Gatehouse names four: senior project manager, programme manager, project director and commercial lead, plus leadership roles within construction organisations and project delivery teams. Those are the awarding body\'s own words rather than our estimate. It does not publish salary data or employment rates, so we are not offering any. The alternative route it describes is onto a full master\'s programme in construction or project management.</p>', 3],
