            ],
            'faqs' => [
                ['Will I be able to get a job in IT after this?', '<p>Qualifi lists employment in an associated profession as one of three published routes, so it is an intended outcome. Being realistic about it: this is a Level 3 foundation covering a lot of ground at introductory depth, and employers hiring for technical roles usually want either demonstrated skill or a higher qualification. It is most useful as evidence of grounding, combined with things you have actually built, and as the step before Level 4 study.</p>', 1],
                ['Is the subject list six items or seven?', '<p>Honestly, Qualifi\'s page is unclear. The unit list prints "Coding and Website Development Networks" on one line, which reads either as a single combined subject or as two separate ones. The overview on the same page lists coding, website development and networks as distinct topics, which is why we have shown them separately. The Centre Specification is the authority, and your centre should confirm the exact count before you enrol.</p>', 2],
                ['Do I need to be able to code already?', '<p>No. Coding is taught within the award and the published outcome is to understand the purpose of coding and the different types in use, which is an introductory framing rather than an expectation of fluency. If you already code and want depth, a Level 3 overview may be too broad for you and Qualifi\'s Level 4 and Level 5 IT diplomas with networking, web design or e-commerce routes would fit better.</p>', 3],
                ['Can I apply with no qualifications?', '<p>You may be able to. Entry runs through a centre interview and applicants must be at least sixteen. Qualifi also allows people with considerable experience but no formal qualifications to be considered, subject to interview and to showing they can cope with the programme. Where English is not your first language, IELTS 6 or equivalent applies, and two supporting references are normally expected.</p>', 4],
                ['What equipment will I need?', '<p>Qualifi does not publish any equipment requirements, which is not the same as there being none. A qualification covering coding, web development and networks will involve practical work, and whether the centre provides machines and software or expects you to have your own varies. Ask before enrolling, because it can change the real cost noticeably.</p>', 5],
                ['How does it compare with the Level 5 extended diplomas in IT?', '<p>It sits two levels below them and is far broader. Qualifi\'s Level 5 extended range splits into separate awards for information technology, networking, web design, e-commerce and cyber security, each going considerably deeper in one direction. This qualification is the survey you take first if you do not yet know which of those you want.</p>', 6],
            ],
            'meta_title' => 'Level 3 Diploma in Information Technology | Qualifi, UK',
            'meta_description' => 'Qualifi Level 3 Diploma in Information Technology. Computer systems, coding, networks, mobile, cyber security and social media. 60 credits. QAN 610/0659/2.',
