            ],
            'faqs' => [
                ['Can I really go straight into the final year of a degree?', '<p>That is the route Qualifi publishes, and 240 credits at Level 5 is why. What it cannot do is hand you the place. The university decides whether to admit you, which course it will admit you to, and what else it wants to see. Qualifi spells that caveat out in black and white elsewhere in its Level 5 range. Approach the universities you are interested in early and ask them directly.</p>', 1],
                ['I have no qualifications, only years of managing people. Is that enough?', '<p>Possibly, yes. Qualifi lists work experience at a managerial level, together with ambition and clear career goals, as an entry route standing on its own. It does not ask for a certificate alongside it. What it does not define is how many years count, so the judgement falls to the approved centre reviewing your application. Set out your responsibilities plainly and let them assess it.</p>', 2],
                ['Is there an age limit or an English test?', '<p>Not on this page. Qualifi publishes three entry bullets here and none mentions age or IELTS, even though several of its other Level 5 diplomas state 18 and over with IELTS 6. We are not going to fill that silence with another award\'s rules. Ask your centre what it applies in practice, because centres can set their own admission checks on top of Qualifi\'s.</p>', 3],
                ['What separates this from the Level 3 business management diploma?', '<p>Two levels and four times the size. The Level 3 award is 60 credits, introduces the subject and exits to a Level 4 certificate or the start of a degree. This is 240 credits, assumes you are already working at or near management, adds leadership as a full theme, and exits at the far end of a degree instead of the beginning.</p>', 4],
                ['Are all twelve subjects compulsory?', '<p>The page lists twelve and does not mark any as optional, nor does it publish credit values for individual subjects. So we cannot tell you whether there is choice inside the programme or how the 240 credits are split. Qualifi\'s combined specification for its business diplomas holds that detail, and your centre can walk you through it before you enrol.</p>', 5],
                ['Timescale and price — where do those come from?', '<p>Not from the awarding body. Qualifi puts no duration on this award and no fee, and unusually it does not publish a total qualification time either, so there is not even a notional hours figure to reason from. Both answers come from the approved centre delivering the teaching, since Qualifi writes and regulates the qualification but runs no classes itself. Get the duration, the intake dates and the full price in writing.</p>', 6],
            ],
