            'hero' => 'Twelve subjects taking you from economics and bookkeeping mathematics through financial and management accounting to taxation, reporting, governance and corporate responsibility. Each published subject has a matching learning outcome, which makes the scope unusually easy to check.',
            'overview' => [
                'Finance roles split in two fairly early. One side reports outwards — statutory accounts, tax returns, the numbers auditors and regulators see. The other side reports inwards, producing the figures managers use to decide things. A great many people learn one half on the job and never formally meet the other. This award covers both.',
                'Qualifi states the aim as giving learners an understanding of management accounting and finance and their role in business, and developing practical skills for a career managing business finances. The subject list follows that through: accounting in a business context, economics, accounting methods, financial accounting, management accounting, financial management, planning and control, financial reporting, taxation, leadership in accounting, management of people, and ethics and corporate responsibility.',
                'Two features set it apart from the three-subject Level 3 award. It adds leadership and people management, acknowledging that senior finance work involves running a function rather than only producing numbers. And ethics gets its own subject. In total it runs to 240 credits at Level 5 and is catalogued as 610/3329/7.',
