            'faqs' => [
                ['Will this exempt me from ACCA or CIMA papers?', '<p>Qualifi publishes no exemptions from any professional accountancy body for this qualification, so we cannot tell you that it does. Exemption decisions belong to the bodies themselves and they assess qualifications individually, sometimes revising their position over time. If exemptions are part of why you are considering this, contact the body with the qualification number before enrolling and get the answer in writing.</p>', 1],
                ['Two of the subject titles look wrong. What is going on?', '<p>They do, and we have left the problem visible rather than papering over it. Qualifi\'s page prints "Economics for Business Mathematical" and "Accounting Methods" as consecutive items, which almost certainly means the line break fell inside the wrong title. Its own learning outcomes mention economics and mathematical skills as separate things. We have shown the sensible reading and flagged it — your centre can confirm against the Centre Specification.</p>', 2],
                ['Do I need accounting experience to start?', '<p>Qualifi publishes no prior qualification requirement and no experience requirement for this award. You must be 18 or over, meet IELTS 6 if English is not your first language, and normally supply two references. Beyond that, it falls to the approved centre to judge whether the workload is realistic for you. That said, the content moves quickly into financial reporting and taxation, so some exposure to accounts will help.</p>', 3],
                ['What does "subject to acceptance by the awarding institution" mean?', '<p>It is Qualifi\'s own wording beside the degree route, and it is refreshingly direct. The awarding body is saying plainly that it can point to where the qualification is designed to lead, while the university or college at the other end sets its own admission criteria and applies them to you. Treat the route as a well-founded possibility to investigate with specific institutions, not as an arrangement already in place.</p>', 4],
                ['How does this compare with the Level 3 accounting diploma?', '<p>The Level 3 award is three subjects and 60 credits, covering transaction record-keeping, cost information and record maintenance. This is twelve subjects and 240 credits, reaching into economics, financial reporting, taxation, governance, people management and ethics. One gives you the grounding for an accounts assistant role; this prepares you for responsibility over a function.</p>', 5],
                ['Is any of it about a specific country\'s tax rules?', '<p>Qualifi titles the subject "Principles and Practices of Taxation" and its outcome refers to the principles of taxation and the requirements of personal and business tax, without naming a jurisdiction. Expect principles that transfer rather than a line-by-line guide to one country\'s tax code. If you need the rules of a specific country, you will want local training alongside this.</p>', 6],
            ],
