            'gcc_heading' => 'Why This Combination Works in the Gulf',
            'gcc' => [
                ['icon' => 'network', 'title' => 'Infrastructure is being built now', 'text' => 'Data centres and national digital infrastructure projects across the GCC need people who can design and secure networks.'],
                ['icon' => 'shield-half', 'title' => 'Smaller teams wear both hats', 'text' => 'In many regional organisations the same team runs the network and defends it, which is exactly this skill mix.'],
                ['icon' => 'wrench', 'title' => 'Hands-on rather than strategic', 'text' => 'Suited to people who want to do the work rather than chair the response.'],
                ['icon' => 'door-open', 'title' => 'No qualification barrier published', 'text' => 'Entry asks for age, English and references only, making it reachable for self-taught practitioners.'],
                ['icon' => 'arrow-up-right', 'title' => 'A published route to Level 7', 'text' => 'Qualifi lists its Level 7 diplomas as the onward step, skipping Level 6 entirely.'],
                ['icon' => 'badge-check', 'title' => 'Vendor certificates are separate', 'text' => 'Cisco and CompTIA routes are not part of this. Budget for them separately if your employer expects them.'],
            ],
            'faqs' => [
                ['What is the difference between this and the cyber security diploma?', '<p>Think of it as the same security core with a different second half bolted on. Both awards teach the seven defensive subjects. Where the standalone cyber security diploma then turns towards the boardroom, this one turns towards the server room: you study hardware and cabling, run systems, move traffic between networks and design the estate rather than preparing statements and leading a response. The honest test is whether you would rather be in the meeting or at the console.</p>', 1],
                ['Why does Qualifi list other qualification numbers on the page?', '<p>Because it is telling you where the content came from. The overview names four existing Qualifi awards — cyber security at Levels 4 and 5, IT networking at Levels 4 and 5 — and gives each number. This is a merged qualification rather than a newly written one. Most awarding bodies do not disclose that, and it means you can see precisely what the combination contains before enrolling.</p>', 2],
                ['There are no learning outcomes on the official page. Why?', '<p>We noticed, and we are telling you rather than filling the gap. Qualifi\'s page carries a link to an outcomes section but no outcomes are printed. Since inventing them would mean putting words in the awarding body\'s mouth, the coverage shown on this page is described from Qualifi\'s stated aim and its published subject list, and is labelled as such. The Centre Specification should carry the formal outcomes.</p>', 3],
                ['Does it match any Cisco or CompTIA certification?', '<p>Nothing published says so. The content clearly overlaps with what vendor certifications cover — routing, switching, network design, security fundamentals — but overlap is not alignment, and Qualifi makes no claim of mapping, exemption or recognition. If your employer or your target role expects a specific certification, plan to take it separately rather than expecting this to count towards it.</p>', 4],
                ['What does the entry requirement actually ask for?', '<p>Less than you might expect. You need to be 18 or over, meet IELTS 6 or equivalent if English is not your first language, and normally provide two references with one preferably academic. No prior qualification is listed and no experience clause appears. That makes it more open on paper than the cyber security award, which asks for Level 3 qualifications, relevant experience or a Level 4 in another field.</p>', 5],
                ['How much of it is actually networking?', '<p>Four subjects out of eleven sit on the infrastructure side; the remaining seven are security. So the weighting favours security, with enough hardware, administration and design content to keep it grounded in real equipment rather than diagrams. Anyone wanting networking as the main event, with general IT underneath it, will find Qualifi\'s IT-Networking award the better match.</p>', 6],
            ],
            'meta_title' => 'Level 5 Diploma in Networking & Cyber Security | Qualifi',
            'meta_description' => 'Qualifi Level 5 Extended Diploma in Networking and Cyber Security. 240 credits, 11 subjects merging security and infrastructure. QAN 610/3042/9.',
        ],
