            'hero' => 'Six core units everybody takes, then one specialism you pick yourself — general management, HR, finance, marketing or projects. The way in is a conversation with the centre, not a form. One hundred and twenty credits at postgraduate level.',
            'overview' => [
                'Strategy courses tend to hand everyone the same syllabus and hope it lands. This one splits in two. Six units are fixed, so every learner covers strategic marketing, finance for managers, strategic direction, strategic planning, creative and innovative management, and corporate responsibility in the wider business environment. After that you pick a lane.',
                'Five specialism routes are published: general management, human resources management, finance, marketing, and project management. Pick project management and you study planning, controlling and leading a project, procurement risk and contract management, and advanced project and logistics management. Pick general management and you take research methods plus development as a strategic manager. The choice is yours and it changes what the qualification means on your CV.',
                'Admission works differently here too. Qualifi states that entry is through a centre interview, with a Level 6 qualification or a first degree expected alongside it, and it leaves a door open for managers with considerable experience but nothing on paper. It is worth 120 credits at Level 7, registered on the framework as 603/5745/9.',
