            'hero' => 'Six units fixed, two chosen from four — finance, marketing, change or workforce planning. Of the four Qualifi strategy diplomas at this level, this is the one that lets you plug the specific gap in your own role.',
            'overview' => [
                'Six mandatory units set the spine. Manage team performance to support strategy. Information management and strategic decision taking. Leading a strategic management project. Strategic direction. Strategic planning. Development as a strategic manager. Read them in order and they describe a working method: decide where to go, plan it, get the information right, lead a project that proves it, and grow into the person who can keep doing that.',
                'Then you add two units from four — finance for managers, strategic marketing, organisational change strategies, or human resource planning. That choice is the practical argument for this award over its siblings. A plant manager short on commercial vocabulary takes finance and marketing; a leader facing a restructure takes change strategies and workforce planning. Nobody carries units they will never use.',
                'Two of the mandatory six deserve a mention on their own. Leading a Strategic Management Project means applied work rather than essays about other people\'s companies. Development as a Strategic Manager turns your own growth into something assessed, which is rare. It is a 120-credit award at Level 7, registered as 601/5335/0.',
