            'is_active' => false,
            'hero' => 'Twelve subjects, and four of them follow the money and the goods: procurement, contracts, logistics, global supply chain. Entry is more formally gated than any sibling award at this level, with an age floor, references and a language test.',
            'overview' => [
                'Plenty of project qualifications stop at method — schedules, critical path, a stage gate diagram. This one runs to twelve subjects and keeps going past the method into the parts that actually derail delivery. Procurement risk and contract management. Project and logistics management. Operations and global supply chain management. Finance for project managers. Four subjects about money moving and goods arriving.',
                'Risk gets two separate treatments: once through procurement and contracts, once through a subject devoted to managing risk, uncertainty and complexity in projects. Alongside those sit planning, controlling and leading a project, operations and information management, leadership and professional development, innovation in project management, and research methods. Qualifi also lists two subjects called Principles of Project Management and Project Management, without explaining how they differ.',
                'What Qualifi says it wants from a learner is ambitious: critical insight into leading-edge practice, autonomy enough to plan and run consultancy projects in a group, originality in approaching complex issues. Accreditation sits at Level 7, the credit value is 120, and the framework number is 610/1342/0. Its specification was reissued in April 2025, making it one of the freshest documents in the range.',
