            'overview' => [
                'Here is a small thing that says a lot. Across much of Qualifi\'s catalogue, the published learning outcomes repeat the same general management sentences with one noun swapped. Not on this page. Nine outcomes appear, every one of them written about marketing: formulating value propositions in provider and customer relationships, assessing market-sourced data for strategic decisions, evaluating creative approaches to product and service design.',
                'Six subjects sit underneath. Contemporary Issues and Principles of Marketing, then Consumer Behaviour and Market Communications, Digital and Social Media Marketing, Contemporary Challenges and Strategic Marketing, Strategic Brand Management, and finally a Marketing Research Project. Qualifi describes the teaching as an integrated approach, pairing theory in marketing, branding, consumer behaviour and digital communication with practice through what it calls real-time activities.',
