            'hero' => 'Written, in Qualifi\'s own words, for managers with the authority to turn organisational strategy into operational performance. Six subjects, from safety culture to sustainability and ethics, closing with a research project you plan yourself.',
            'overview' => [
                'Awarding bodies rarely describe their intended reader this precisely. Qualifi says this diploma develops safety management skills for managers who have the authority and the personal attributes to translate organisational strategy into effective operational performance. That sentence does a lot of work. It is not aimed at the person carrying out inspections; it is aimed at the person who decides what the organisation\'s safety position is and then has to make it real.',
                'Six subjects follow that logic. Health and Safety Management Practice. Effectiveness of Health and Safety Management Systems. Factors Affecting Risk and Strategic Risk Intervention. Strategic Commitment to Health and Well-Being. Sustainability and Ethics in Health and Safety Practice. Advanced Research Methods. Notice how far the last two sit from a hazard checklist — ethics and sustainability are treated as part of the safety professional\'s remit, not as a separate corporate exercise.',
